smithy doctor: check everything a warden batch needs (--quiet: problems only;
--fix [--yes]: apply fixes)

usage: smithy doctor [--quiet] [--fix [--yes]]
Checks everything a warden batch needs, one line per check; --quiet prints
problems only. --fix lists each fix that changes only your own files (exact
change shown) and applies it on y; --yes applies all but permission grants
(those need y); without a terminal and without --yes it applies none. Exit 1
when a check failed (the checks run before any fix).

Examples:
  smithy doctor
  smithy doctor --quiet
  smithy doctor --fix

See also: smithy help setup, smithy help version
Exit codes: 0 success, 1 failure, 2 usage error (3 where a command's help says).
